# Cursor Rules - nuri-task-api

Backend only. Do not generate frontend UI, CSS frameworks, or animation libraries in this repo.

## Stack

Express 5 (ESM) + Mongoose 8 + MongoDB + JWT + Nodemailer + Vercel serverless.

- Identifiers, files, types: English.
- Comments and JSDoc: Spanish, concise. Never `@static`, `@async`, `@function`.
- Layers: `controllers/` → `services/` → `models/` + `models/dtos/`. Controllers stay thin (HTTP in/out). Business logic lives in services.

## ResponseModel

Always return a ResponseModel. Never hardcode `res.status(200).json({...})`.

Shape: `{ success, status, message, data, meta }`.

| Status | Class | When |
|--------|-------|------|
| 200 | `SuccessResponseModel` | GET, PUT, PATCH |
| 201 | `CreatedResponseModel` | POST create |
| 204 | `NoContentResponseModel` | DELETE empty |
| 400 | `BadRequestResponseModel` / `ValidationErrorResponseModel` | Bad input |
| 401 | `UnauthorizedResponseModel` | Missing/invalid token |
| 403 | `ForbiddenResponseModel` | Authenticated, no permission |
| 404 | `NotFoundResponseModel` | Missing resource |
| 409 | `ConflictResponseModel` | Duplicate (email, etc.) |
| 500 | `ErrorResponseModel` | Unexpected |

See https://developer.mozilla.org/es/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Status

```javascript
static async getUser(req, res) {
  const result = await UserService.getUserById(req.params.id);
  return res.status(result.status).json(result);
}
```

Do not pass `req` into a service. Extract `userId`, `params`, `body`, `query`.

## Auth

- `validateToken` — JWT from cookie `nuri_auth` (HttpOnly) or `Authorization: Bearer`.
- `validateAdminToken` — JWT + `isAdmin` from DB (`getRequestUser`).
- `validateSubscription` — premium / admin.
- `validateCronSecret` — cron header vs `CRON_SECRET`.

JWT secret: only `UserServiceHelpers.getJwtSecret()` (throws if missing).

## DTOs

Every HTTP write (and filter query) goes through a DTO.

- `validate()` → `{ isValid, errors }`. `toPlainObject()` → sanitized payload.
- **Zod** owns field rules (`models/dtos/zodHelpers.js` + `static schema`). `validate()` calls `validateZod`.
- **Inheritance** when fields are shared: `schema.extend(...)`, `super(data)`, reuse `toPlainObject`.
- Never suffix `Response` on a DTO (`UserDto`, `MinTodoDto`, `CreateUserDto`). Sanitize outputs with helpers (004).
- Query booleans: `queryBooleanField` (`true` / `false` / `"true"` / `"false"`). Do **not** use `z.coerce.boolean()` (`"false"` would become `true`).
- No DTO for Mercado Pago webhook body (HMAC) or cron payloads.

```javascript
export class CreateAdminUserDto extends CreateUserDto {
  static schema = CreateUserDto.schema.extend({
    isAdmin: z.boolean().optional(),
  });

  constructor(data) {
    super(data);
    this.isAdmin = data.isAdmin || false;
  }

  validate() {
    return validateZod(this.constructor.schema, this);
  }
}
```

STOP if a new DTO duplicates an existing one — extend it.

## JSDoc

One-line description. `@param` type + short note. `@returns` type only.

```javascript
/**
 * Obtiene un usuario por ID
 * @param {string} id
 * @returns {Promise<SuccessResponseModel|NotFoundResponseModel|ErrorResponseModel>}
 */
```

## Errors

Services return ResponseModels. Use `ErrorHandler.handleDatabaseError`. Early returns. No swallowed invariants (016). Side-effects (achievements/push) may swallow; counters must not.

## Indexes / pagination

Listings: sort `{ _id: sortOrder }`, cursor = last `_id`. Declare indexes on the schema; Mongoose `autoIndex` creates them on boot.

## Env

Read `.env.example` and the README env table. Never commit `.env`. Never put a usable JWT/MP/VAPID secret in examples.

